const aboutParagraphs = [
  `I spend my days as a Data Analyst turning raw production data — timelines, budgets, salary structures for 500+ employees — into decisions people actually act on. That same instinct for turning raw signal into action pulled me into infrastructure: I've built and run Kubernetes clusters on bare metal and in the cloud, with full observability and alerting that catches problems before they become outages. I've replaced manual deployments with GitOps, wired up CI/CD pipelines with testing and vulnerability scanning baked in, and I write up my production incidents publicly.`,
  `That curiosity didn't come from one place. Environmental Science was my undergrad — physics, chemistry, biology, geology, statistics pulling together — and it's where I first learned how things work together as systems. Day to day, I work with databases and Power Query, automating manual processes wherever I can. It was that combination — systems thinking on one side, the itch to automate on the other — that really sparked my curiosity, and I've been building up my skills to make the jump ever since. With help from KubeCraft, a DevOps mentorship community, I taught myself Kubernetes, Docker, CI/CD, Python, and Linux. Now I'm looking for roles where I get to work hands-on with cloud infrastructure and Kubernetes at scale.`,
  `When I'm not at the desk learning, I'm usually outside enjoying the sun or reading philosophy.`,
];

